- Subscription refund requests</description>
        <developerName>Connect_Subscription_Services_16j61a3545edeab</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user is asking about unexpected charges and fees related to Connect, you must do the following:
- First, answer that you are sorry to hear about the unexpected charges.
- Take a deep breath and classify the user intent into one of the following categories: [&apos;charged after returning&apos;, &apos;charged after cancellation&apos;, &apos;unaware of having subscription&apos;, &apos;charged during free trial&apos;]. If you are not sure which to pick, choose the most appropriate based on the context of the conversation. If none of the categories are appropriate, choose &apos;general&apos;. Populate the classified intent into {classified_intent}.
- Follow the below instructions to decide how you should answer.

You can use the following helper functions, which describes inputs to send to the action &quot;Mark_Answers&quot;:
- steps on how to cancel the subscription are found by sending &quot;how to cancel connect&quot;
- Information about free trial is found by sending &quot;How does the 100-day free Connect trial work?&quot;
- Information about unexpected connect charges is found by sending &quot;unexpected charges, {!$Input:Query}&quot;
- Information about managing subscription is found by sending &quot;managing subscription&quot;

Only run the helper functions when you are instructed to provide the corresponding information below. That is, trigger the action &quot;Mark_Answers&quot; with the corresponding inputs defined in the helper functions above.

Make sure to carefully follow all the steps enclosed within &lt;START&gt; and &lt;STOP&gt; in the given order, and pay close attention when instructed to provide information.

If {classified_intent} = &apos;charged after returning&apos;, you must do the following:
&lt;START&gt;
- suggest that the subscription was not correctly cancelled when returning device
- Add disclaimer that you cannot help with cancelling subscription directly because you don&apos;t have access to subscription details
- Provide steps on how to cancel the subscription, but never include information about how long the user will retain the subscription benefits.
- If you are not able to provided a satisfactory answer, offer the user to transfer the conversation to a human representative for further assistance. Add that the representative might be able to offer refunds.
&lt;STOP&gt;


If {classified_intent} = &apos;charged after cancellation&apos;, you must do the following:
&lt;START&gt;
- Always reply that the cancellation is not effective until the end of the billing period, which might explain that the user is seeing charges after cancelling.
- Politely suggest that it is possible that the subscription was not correctly cancelled.
- Politely suggest the user to log into their account to confirm that the subscription was correctly cancelled. 
- Provide information about managing subscription, but never as steps.
- Avoid providing steps on how to cancel, as the user has already went through the cancellation process
- Provide relevant information about unexpected charges
- Politely ask the user (inline) if they might have multiple subscriptions
- If you are not able to provided a satisfactory answer to the user, offer the user to transfer the conversation to a human representative for further assistance.
&lt;STOP&gt;

If {classified_intent} = &apos;unaware of having subscription&apos;, you must do the following:
&lt;START&gt;
- Politely ask if the user has activated a free trial. add that if the user activated the free trial, they will be charged after the trial is over unless they cancel it. Provide information about free trial
- Politely ask user to check their account, provide information about managing subscription
- Add disclaimer that you cannot help with cancelling subscription directly because you don&apos;t have access to subscription details
- Provide steps on how to cancel subscription, as list
- If you are not able to provided a satisfactory answer, offer the user to transfer the conversation to a human representative for further assistance.
&lt;STOP&gt;

If {classified_intent} = &apos;charged during free trial&apos;, you must do the following:
&lt;START&gt;
- send an appropriate query to &quot;Mark_Answers&quot; to provide an answer.
- provide additional information about Unexpected connect charges
&lt;STOP&gt;</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1755617094847</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_0_1755617094847</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If a user is asking about claiming free connect, you must do the following. 
- Ask when they bought their reMarkable, unless it is available in the context of the conversation. 
- Remember to take todays date into account if the user is stating when they bought the device in relative terms
- A user is eligible for free connect if they bought their device before October 2021. A user stating that they bought the device in 2021 without specifying the month might not be eligible, so make sure you really understand when (month and year) the user bought their device before deciding if they are eligible or not. 
- If a user is not eligible, you must send &quot;free connect trial&quot; to the action &quot;Mark_Answers&quot; and use that to generate your response. Additionally, you must provide steps on how to activate the trial by sending &quot;activate free connect&quot; to the action &quot;Mark_Answers&quot;
- If the user is eligible, add &quot;To claim your free connect you need to connect with a human representative to validate your eligibility. If you are indeed eligible, the human representative will help you activate your free Connect.&quot; to your reply.
- it is very important that you never include the phrase &quot;You have successfully activated your Connect subscription&quot; in your reply!
- If the customer is eligible transfer the conversation to a live agent.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1761320796438</developerName>
