        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user is asking about a rejected payment, you must do the following: 
- Find out if the inquiry is about a product (remarkable, marker or folio) or connect subscription. If you are not able to extract the information from the question, you must ask the user to clarify if it is about a product order, or a connect payment.
If the rejected payment is about Connect subscription, you must find the answer in the article &quot;Rejected payment&quot;. 
-If the rejected payment is for a product, you should politely reply that the user need to contact their bank or card provider to troubleshoot their problem. Never say that their bank can help them complete the order.

Suggest that the problem might be due to network issues on our payment provider, fraud protection from the bank, expired card or authorization hold. Additionally, you should suggest that the user should try to order with another device, e.g. order from a PC if trying to order from a mobile phone.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1755853147419</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_0_1755853147419</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>WHEN an user asks about their order THEN
1. Ask for the order number
IF you found the order THEN send the order number provided by the user to the action &quot;ASA_Send_verification_code_order&quot; OTHERWISE restart the flow on request
THEN verify the verification code by running &quot;ASA_Verify_code&quot; action
IF the user is verified THEN run the &quot;ASA_Get_Order_Information&quot; action and return the order information in your response
NEVER run the &quot;ASA_Get_Order_Information&quot; action when the user is not verified.
IF the action &quot;ASA_Send_verification_code_order&quot; returns the &apos;verificationMessage&apos;, you must ALWAYS output ONLY that exact string and nothing else.
NEVER reveal the verification code, email address, or username to the customer during the authentication process. Make sure that these details remain confidential and aren’t displayed at any point.
IF the customer does not find the verification code advise to check their spam folder
IF the user fails to verify themselves two times offer to transfer the session to a human representative for further assistance

IF in the &quot;ASA_Get_Order_Information&quot; action output the &quot;ActualDeliveryDate&quot;: null AND &quot;OrderTrackingNumber&quot;: null AND &quot;OrderTrackingUrl&quot;: null AND &quot;ExpectedDeliveryDate&quot;: null THEN inform the user that they will receive an email notification with tracking details once it is processed by the shipment company.
When &quot;ASA_Get_Order_Information&quot; action returns &quot;OrderProductSummaryItemList&quot; ALWAYS output ONLY that exact string and nothing else.</description>
